# FDD 07 review — "07 - Credit Card Payments and Refunds" (Features 7.1, 7.2, 7.3).
# Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Payments graph
# (payments-capability.ttl / payments-permissions.ttl / payments-api.ttl /
# payments-sequences.ttl / payments-technical-design.ttl, all loaded together), which is a
# very close match: this FDD is essentially the source functional spec that
# payments-capability.md/payments-sequences.md were themselves derived from, so most
# numbered stories here map onto an already-modeled Sequence/Rule/Operation with high
# confidence rather than a speculative one.
#
# Source: "7 - Credit card payments and Refunds-.docx" (Epic 187622). Read the .md sibling
# first, then unzipped the .docx for comments.xml/commentsExtended.xml (30 comments, 6 in
# threads via w15:paraIdParent, the rest standalone) and word/media (16 images, image1-6
# are .png "Screenshots" from the main Business Specifications section, image7-16 are .jpg
# higher-fidelity Addendum screenshots for Features 7.1/7.3) — all 16 were individually
# viewed (small enough set that full depth was practical; see CONVENTIONS.md's "not every
# image needs viewing" guidance, not invoked here since there was no need to sample).
#
# Companion documents also present in this FDD folder and read for corroborating detail
# (NOT separately promoted into their own Requirement set — they describe the CEPAS
# interface contract itself, which payments-capability.ttl/payments-technical-design.ttl
# already model in full; used here only to confirm or add nuance to the numbered stories
# below): "7.0 CEPAS/Interface Design document - CEPAS (Payments).md" (AES-GCM encryption
# spec, SHA-1 hash calculation, confirmation query-string field layout — matches
# pay:TP_CepasRedirectInitiation/TP_CepasConfirmationProcessing exactly), "...CEPAS
# (Reimbursements).md" (POST /api/v1/payment/cancel field layout — matches
# pay:TP_CepasRefundApiCall), "...CEPAS (Posting File).md" (fixed-width AH/AD/AF record
# layout — matches pay:BatchJob_PostingFileReconciliation's own notes). "Payments/Payment_
# flow.vsdx" and "Payments/CEPAS Integration/CEPAS flow.vsdx"/".pdf" skipped per
# CONVENTIONS.md's vsdx-skip rule (payments-sequences.ttl's mermaid content is a fuller,
# already-converted equivalent). "Payments/Payments_Scenarios.xlsx" was read (not
# vsdx/pptx, and short) — six informal scenario rows, five of which just restate content
# already in the main document; the sixth ("Paying for a Permit after school year ends")
# is genuinely new and is captured as pay:Question_PostSchoolYearPaymentValidation below.
# "MOECS Current Process Documentation" (.doc/.pdf/.msg) skipped — legacy reference
# material for the predecessor system, not load-bearing for MiEdWorkforce's own design
# (image1.png, one of the 16 embedded images, turns out to BE a MOECS legacy screenshot
# reused inline — see cred:... no, pay:WireframeLegacyMoecs below — corroborating that
# these documents are backward-reference material, not new requirements).
#
# Structure of the document and what's used as the Requirement unit:
# - A "Business Specifications" prose section covers both payments AND refunds in detail
#   (inbound/outbound data elements for both, CEPAS-down handling, posting-file
#   reconciliation, bulk/batch processing) plus a 16-row "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" paraphrase
#   table restating the same ground — the HLS table is skipped per CONVENTIONS.md.
# - An "Addendum" with real Feature/story numbering (7.1.1-7.1.5, 7.2.1-7.2.3, 7.3.1-7.3.2 —
#   10 stories total) is the primary Requirement unit used below.
# - Exactly like FDD 29's own pilot finding, the Addendum's numbering OMITS an entire
#   real, wireframed capability the Business Specifications prose describes in detail:
#   refund processing by the Credential Administrator (its own inbound/outbound data-
#   element tables, and HLS Use Cases 9-11) never got a 7.1.x/7.2.x/7.3.x number anywhere
#   in the Addendum, even though Feature 7.1's own title is "CEPAS Interface (Payments AND
#   REFUNDS)". Modeled below with a synthetic pay:Req_07_BizSpec_Refund ID and flagged as a
#   discrepancy (pay:Question_AddendumOmitsRefundFeature), rather than silently folded into
#   7.1's numbering or silently dropped.
# - Feature 7.2/7.3's own numbering has no internal inconsistency (unlike FDD 29's 29.4)
#   and needed no synthetic IDs or renumbering.
#
# Comments: 30 total (28 from the original 2025 review cycle, dated 2025-06-26 through
# 2026-01-16; 2 much later standalone ones dated 2026-03-06 — see below). Most are
# minor wording-confirmation exchanges ("Updated", "Added") already resolved in-thread and
# folded into the relevant story's own sd:notes rather than transcribed. Two threads
# surfaced a substantive, still-live finding and are modeled as standalone Annotations:
# - Comments 7/8/9 (Caswell asking whether Success/Error messaging appears in
#   MiEdWorkforce itself; Punniyamoorthy replying "MiEd will not display any message
#   related to payment, but will change the status"; Caswell noting the visible document
#   text contradicts that explanation and that wording was edited to match — with no
#   further reply confirming the edit was accepted) — this is a genuine, still-open
#   contradiction between what the FDD's own prose/wireframes show (an explicit Payment
#   Successful/Payment Error page — see wireframes 04/10/11/15/16 below, all showing
#   dedicated MiEdWorkforce-rendered success/error content) and what its own author says
#   the system actually does. See pay:Question_PaymentResultMessagingContradiction below,
#   modeled on FDD 29's Question_CoverLetterStoryContradiction precedent.
# - Comments 132877093/1640280882 (Caswell, dated 2026-03-06 — six weeks after every other
#   comment in the document and seven months after the 08/01/2025 approval signoff),
#   flagging a dead hyperlink ("brings you to a 'Page not found' message") and an access
#   request ("Can access be granted for these?") on the Additional Resources links
#   (Payment_flow.vsdx / CEPAS_BestPractices.doc / Consumer Payments Integration Guide),
#   both with no reply. Document-hygiene only, not a functional finding — noted here (same
#   as FDD 29's own post-signoff-revision finding) so the approval table isn't read as
#   "nothing changed after this," but not modeled as its own Annotation.
# - Comment 10 ("Define users.") on 7.1.1's "As a User (Citizen, Business, State Admin)"
#   phrasing is the same kind of role-definition thread FDD 11/16 and 29 both already
#   surfaced; here it's a single unreplied comment rather than a multi-comment thread, and
#   payments-permissions.md/payments-sequences.md already resolve "Business User" concretely
#   (district staff managing temporary credentials/substitutes) — folded into 7.1.1's notes
#   rather than re-raised as a new Annotation.
# - Comment 30/31 (Punniyamoorthy/Caswell): "Payment Type" (Credit Card or Bank Remittance)
#   added as a data element mid-review. Folded into 7.1.4's notes as a minor terminology
#   nuance against pay:PaymentConfirmation's existing "card type" field, not a new gap.
#
# Tracked changes: not separately reconstructed (no comment thread here depends on a
# stale-vs-corrected text distinction the way FDD 29's Confirm-Enrollment thread did).
#
# Wireframes: all 16 embedded images viewed and extracted to wireframes/. image1.png-
# image6.png (the six "Screenshot N" images the Business Specifications section refers to
# by number, skipping "Screenshot 4" in the source's own numbering — an unexplained gap,
# not investigated further given how minor it is) are data-flow/sequence diagrams and
# lower-fidelity mockups; image7.jpg-image16.jpg are higher-fidelity Addendum screenshots
# of an actual Career Authorization Application's Payment tab and a "District staff"-facing
# Unpaid Application Fees screen. Confirmed by viewing, not assumed from document order —
# in particular image1.png (Screenshot 4's neighbor) turned out to be a legacy MOECS system
# screenshot reused as reference material, not a proposed MiEdWorkforce screen; caught only
# by actually looking at it (its own on-screen text says "log on to MOECS System").
#
# Cross-domain note: this FDD's own Dependencies section names five OTHER FDDs by number
# (1.0 auth/roles = iam, 2.0 Reports = reporting, 3.0 Dashboards = dashboards, 4.0 Business
# Rule Management = pay-fee-link availability rules, 5.1-5.3 System Administration =
# credentialing fee/global-parameter config, 6.0 Alerts/Emails/Communications = comm).
# None of these dependencies are modeled as Requirements of THIS FDD (they're the other
# FDDs' own subject matter) — noted only where a numbered story here directly references
# one (7.1.1's email template -> comm:EmailTemplateAggregate).

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix pay:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:payments:> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix comm:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:> .
@prefix ext:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

pay:Fdd07Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/07 - Credit Card Payments and Refunds/7 - Credit card payments and Refunds-.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 7.1-7.3 (the document's own subtitle: '7.0 Credit Card Payments/Refunds (7.1, 7.2 and 7.3)'). Author Vidhya Punniyamoorthy (DTMB); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/01/2025 per the signoff table — but two comments (132877093/1640280882) are dated 2026-03-06, over seven months after signoff, flagging a dead Additional-Resources hyperlink and an access request. Not resolved here (document hygiene, not a functional finding); noted so the signoff table isn't read as 'nothing changed after this' — same caution FDD 29's own header carries for the same reason." .

pay:Fdd07CepasPaymentsInterfaceDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "review" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/07 - Credit Card Payments and Refunds/7.0 CEPAS/Interface Design document - CEPAS (Payments).docx" ;
    sd:notes "CEPAS's own interface contract: AES-256-GCM redirect payload encryption (amount/id/ref/returnurl plaintext, 12-byte nonce, 16-byte tag), and the SHA-1(ConfirmationNumber+Amount+SecurityKey) hash-validation formula for the return redirect. Confirms pay:TP_CepasRedirectInitiation and pay:TP_CepasConfirmationProcessing in payments-capability.ttl match the actual interface spec field-for-field; not separately modeled as its own Requirement set." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .

pay:Fdd07CepasReimbursementsInterfaceDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "review" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/07 - Credit Card Payments and Refunds/7.0 CEPAS/Interface Design document - CEPAS (Reimbursements).docx" ;
    sd:notes "CEPAS's CancelPayment API contract (Header: ApplicationID/PaymentChannel/SecurityKey; body: ConfirmationNumber/RefundAmount). Confirms pay:TP_CepasRefundApiCall in payments-capability.ttl matches the actual interface spec; not separately modeled." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .

pay:Fdd07CepasPostingFileInterfaceDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "review" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/07 - Credit Card Payments and Refunds/7.0 CEPAS/Interface Design document - CEPAS (Posting File).docx" ;
    sd:notes "Fixed-width AH (header)/AD (transaction detail)/AF (footer) posting-file layout, retrieved via SFTP. Confirms pay:BatchJob_PostingFileReconciliation's own notes on the file format; also the ultimate source of the Payment Command Code vocabulary already captured verbatim as pay:UT_PaymentCommandCode in payments-capability.ttl. Not separately modeled." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .

pay:WireframeDataFlowElements a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/07-credit-card-payments-and-refunds/wireframes/wireframe-01-payment-data-flow-elements.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Screenshot 1' per the document's own caption. A data-flow box diagram (not a UI mockup): Inbound Payment Request (MiEdWorkforce Payment Review screen -> API -> CEPAS, carrying Type of License/Application Reference Number/Payment Amount) and Outbound Payment Response (CEPAS -> API -> MiEdWorkforce Payment Review screen, carrying the full outbound element list). Directly corroborates the Business Specifications section's own inbound/outbound data-element tables and 7.1.3/7.1.4." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .
pay:WireframePaymentFlowSequence a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/07-credit-card-payments-and-refunds/wireframes/wireframe-02-payment-flow-sequence-cepas.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Screenshot 2'. An UML-style sequence diagram (Users -> MiEdWorkforce UI -> CEPAS) showing: click Pay -> UI requests encrypted URL from an 'Encryption endpoint' -> UI sends user to CEPAS URL -> user pays at CEPAS -> CEPAS returns success message with HASH -> UI requests a HASH check from a 'Hash-check endpoint' -> UI displays Success/Error message. This is a close match to pay:Seq_IndividualPaymentHappyPath's own mermaid content, down to the encrypt/hash-check endpoint split, and is itself evidence AGAINST comment 8's 'no message displayed' claim — see pay:Question_PaymentResultMessagingContradiction." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .
pay:WireframePaymentReviewSummary a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/07-credit-card-payments-and-refunds/wireframes/wireframe-03-payment-review-summary.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Screenshot 3'. A 'Payment review' screen (Daily Substitute Permit fee, $45.00, payer name) with the CEPAS static-text notice ('Michigan Department of Education uses the CEPAS Credit Card Processing Payment Module...') and Previous/Next navigation — directly corroborates 7.1.2's required pre-redirect static text (comment 18-21 thread)." ;
    sd:definedIn pay:Fdd07Doc .
pay:WireframePaymentSuccessfulScreenshot5 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
